.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-INIT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-init
.Nd make this machine the first control plane of a Kubernetes cluster, with Cilium, MetalLB and ZFS storage
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Run after
.Xr kube-setup 8
on the machine that will be the first control plane.
In order it:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
checks that kubeadm, kubectl, Helm and the Cilium CLI are installed,
containerd is running, and no cluster is already up here;
.It
snapshots every dataset of the root's pool, as
.Ar pool Ns Pa @pre-kube-init- Ns Ar timestamp ,
and warns if it cannot;
.It
when
.Ev KUBE_VIP_ADDRESS
is set, puts that address on the node and runs kube-vip to hold it, so
that other control planes can join behind one address;
.It
runs
.Ql kubeadm init
without kube-proxy, and lets workloads run on the control plane;
.It
installs Cilium, in place of kube-proxy;
.It
installs the Gateway API, MetalLB with an address pool, ZFS LocalPV
storage \(em or local-path storage when the node has no ZFS \(em and
metrics-server, each warned about rather than fatal if it fails;
.It
saves a join command for
.Xr kube-join 8 ,
starts a sample nginx deployment, and prints the cluster's state.
.El
.Pp
Charts, manifests and versions come from
.Pa /root/darksite
when it holds them, so a node with no internet can do all of it.
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Xr kube-cluster 8
runs it on the first control plane it makes.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description and environment and exit 0, without root.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev POD_CIDR , Ev SVC_CIDR
Default
.Ql 10.244.0.0/16
and
.Ql 10.96.0.0/16 .
The service range is a /16, not kubeadm's /12, which covers 10.96 to
10.111 and so many LANs.
.It Ev CILIUM_VERSION , Ev METALLB_VERSION , Ev KUBE_VIP_VERSION
Default the lock's.
.It Ev METALLB_POOL
The LoadBalancer address range; empty takes .200 to .220 of the node's
/24.
.It Ev METALLB_POOL_NAME
Default
.Ql kldload-pool ;
anything that asks for a pool by name must use this one.
.It Ev KUBE_VIP_ADDRESS , Ev KUBE_VIP_INTERFACE
A free address for the API server to share among control planes, and the
interface to hold it; set it now, since the certificates name it.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kubernetes/join-command.sh
The join command, mode 0600.
.It Pa /root/darksite/k8s-stack.lock
The versions the image was built with.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the control plane is up; 1 when a step it cannot do without
failed, named.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Not run for this page, since it makes a cluster:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-init
# METALLB_POOL=192.168.122.230-192.168.122.239 KUBE_VIP_ADDRESS=192.168.122.240 kube-init
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr kube-join 8 ,
.Xr kube-reset 8 ,
.Xr kube-setup 8 ,
.Xr kube-status 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-08-19 the MetalLB pool's name did not match what four other files
asked for, and a first boot waited fifteen minutes on a LoadBalancer
that never came.
On 2026-09-20 it read a version lock that only the host has, and died
before printing anything on every control plane.
On 2026-09-28 the service range moved from /12 to /16 when a route over it
cut nodes off the LAN.
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: its help said an empty
.Ev METALLB_POOL
left MetalLB unconfigured, and a snapshot that failed was logged as the
rollback point.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
On a node with ZFS but no pool named
.Ql rpool ,
it makes one on a 20 GB file,
.Pa /var/lib/zfs-csi-pool.img ,
for the storage driver.
